Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-07-2000||01:23 PM||||Tom,<P>I was wondering if anyone would notice that.  What years are yours?  I like the old 429's and Mach I Mustangs.  Oddly enough my fiancee owns a 93 Mustang, bright yellow with a black convertable top.  I respect the car, but would never consider purchasing one.... mostly because I don't feel like I fit in the car.  I am not a man of large stature at about 6' 185, but I always feel cramped.  Not to mention that my boots (only size 9) hit the bottom of the dash often causing brief, but scary moments where I cannot remove my foot from the gas.  All in all it is a good car though.  Rock solid mechanics in both the engine and suspension.  I hope that you are not offended.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-07-2000||08:23 PM||||This thread wasn't directed to me but I need to insert my $.02 anyway.  I don't know what years of Mustangs you have, Tom, but I think that the newer ones look generic (of course, almost all new cars do.).  I like the older ones, though.  A friend of mine has a pretty cool one.  I don't know much about Mustangs, but his is a 500KR?  I've never heard on one, but it looks good and is not only perfect, but 100% original.  I remember when he bought it and complained about the price the whole time he was washing and waxing it!  (Very expensive--I've owned trucks [18-wheelers] that were cheaper than his car!!)||||reg||1
